WEBVTT

00:00:00.282 --> 00:00:05.109
Here's how to upload your photos and video to a shoot
in REPro Dashboard and

00:00:05.114 --> 00:00:07.105
send everything to the editing team

00:00:08.648 --> 00:00:13.555
From your photographer dashboard open the assigned
shoot Check the property

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:18.413
address then find Raw Uploads Choose Upload Files or

00:00:18.418 --> 00:00:21.015
Upload More if files are already attached

00:00:22.548 --> 00:00:26.743
Drag in your images or RAW files or select them from
your computer

00:00:27.537 --> 00:00:32.261
Match them to the correct booked service Only services
assigned to you

00:00:32.266 --> 00:00:33.149
are available

00:00:34.715 --> 00:00:39.090
For bracketed photography check the Bracket setting
matches what you captured

00:00:39.871 --> 00:00:44.105
Check the selected count and add any instructions in
Notes for Editor

00:00:45.648 --> 00:00:50.075
Choose Confirm and upload or Upload all for a batch
across services

00:00:50.856 --> 00:00:54.175
Keep this browser tab open and wait for Upload
complete

00:00:55.715 --> 00:01:00.568
To add video choose Upload More select your video
clips and check the video

00:01:00.573 --> 00:01:05.325
service Upload them and wait for completion Use the

00:01:05.330 --> 00:01:08.185
matching service for drone and other booked media

00:01:09.748 --> 00:01:14.861
Review the uploaded files and counts If a file failed
retry

00:01:14.866 --> 00:01:19.563
it and confirm it appears before continuing If a file
is rejected

00:01:19.763 --> 00:01:23.262
read the upload result and fix the issue before
retrying

00:01:24.815 --> 00:01:30.133
When everything is attached choose Submit Raw Files
Check the confirmation

00:01:30.255 --> 00:01:35.172
then select Yes submit This sets the shoot status to
Uploaded

00:01:35.177 --> 00:01:37.078
and notifies the editing team

00:01:38.648 --> 00:01:43.373
You're done Upload first review every file then submit

00:01:44.152 --> 00:01:48.231
You can replay this guide from Upload guide on your
photographer dashboard
